"""Integrate the approved marine update into the existing 31-section specification."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,re

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent

def prefix(file,text):
    p=ROOT/file;s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8');title,rest=s.split('\n',1)
    if '## Marine economy, disease and valuation — 2026-10-13' not in s:
        p.write_text(title+'\n\n## Marine economy, disease and valuation — 2026-10-13\n\n'+text+'\n\n'+rest,encoding='utf8')

mdp=ROOT/'MASTER_DEVELOPMENT_PROMPT.md';s=mdp.read_text(encoding='utf8')
if '## 9.3.1 Current Marine Disease, Examination and Treatment' not in s:
    assert re.findall(r'^# (\d+)\.',s,re.M)==[str(n) for n in range(1,32)]
    s=s.replace('VERSION 2.7','VERSION 2.8',1)
    s=s.replace('### Revision: 2.7 consolidates the dedicated clownfish collection, saltwater scope lock, physical coral mounting, shared store redesign and permanent destination-aquarium rule.',
                '### Revision: 2.8 integrates the approved offline marine economy, disease, diagnosis, quarantine, medicine and valuation update. All 31 major sections and prior locked rules remain preserved.')
    s=s.replace('The active development phase is artwork only. Do not expand economy, breeding, chemistry, quests, VIP, stores, black market or new gameplay. Rendering changes are allowed only to display and compare artwork.',
                'This historical art-review phase was artwork only. The later expressly authorized store/collection milestone and current marine economy/disease/valuation milestone supersede that earlier scope gate for their named features. Unrelated gameplay expansion and automatic art approval remain prohibited. Current medical rules are in 9.3.1, valuation in 16.4, medicines in 18.5 and restricted treatments in 19.3.')
    s=s.replace('Freshwater has the same seven categories with Plants instead of Corals.', 'Saltwater additionally has Medicine & Treatment. Freshwater retains its original seven categories with Plants instead of Corals; no new freshwater medicines or disease content are authorized.')
    s=s.replace('Eggs & Specimens, Special Equipment. An empty freshwater category', 'Eggs & Specimens, Special Equipment, Restricted Treatments. An empty freshwater category')
    inserts={
      '## 8.5 Death Artwork':'''### Marine Coral Health Extension

Corals retain individual identity, age, health and mounting and additionally track living tissue, pigment/bleaching, polyp extension, nutrition, examined conditions and treatment history. Distinguish environmental stress, noninfectious bleaching, tissue loss, applicable suspected infectious syndromes and pest damage. Do not assign fish parasites to corals. Broad coral groups do not imply a verified taxon-specific diagnosis. Standard unexamined frags have fixed prices; introduced risk is assigned once at acquisition and saved. Living bleaching can recover; dead tissue has no living asset value. Select the existing appropriate health-state art without replacing artwork.

''',
      '## 9.4 Fish Death Animation':'''## 9.3.1 Current Marine Disease, Examination and Treatment

Implement a centralized data-driven system for marine ich, marine velvet, Brooklynellosis, flukes, selected bacterial syndromes, malnutrition and environmental injury. Define eligible hosts, cause/uncertainty, route, onset, symptoms, severity, contagiousness, damage, diagnosis confidence, treatment, contraindications and recovery. Some conditions are noncontagious. Fish disease must not be assigned to future shrimp, crabs, snails, starfish or urchins; those organisms need separately verified host profiles when authorized. No new invertebrate roster is authorized by this update.

Examination consumes diagnostic supplies and reveals confidence-qualified findings. Visual symptoms alone are not a definitive diagnosis; hidden carriage stays undisclosed until examination. Selected bacterial treatment requires a delayed follow-up and adequate confidence. Negative examinations do not guarantee freedom from disease. Quarantine uses independent prepared/cycled marine water, suitable capacity and coral mounts where applicable. Transfers preserve individual identity and history and revalidate water, social/territory and active-course restrictions.

Treatment consumes owned units exactly once and progresses over time. Effect depends on host, diagnosis, severity, duration, environment and saved product quality. Wrong treatment can fail or harm; there is no universal instant cure. Copper-inspired products require monitored bare fish-only adult quarantine and cannot be administered to reef coral/invertebrates. Use documented veterinary/husbandry references. Clinical concentrations and real-world recipes are not game controls; numeric rates and durations are explicitly accelerated game parameters. Severe disease uses existing fish mortality and coral death states, not a parallel death engine. Preserve the existing freshwater disease/treatment behavior unchanged.

''',
      '# 17. ECONOMY, INCOME & MARKET BALANCING':'''## 16.4 Authoritative Current Livestock and Tank Valuation

Keep fixed retail purchase price, current individual asset value and actual dealer resale offer separate. Every owned fish/coral/bottom dweller has a persistent ID and a bounded current AC value. Consider biological/product baseline, stage, age/size, health, disease severity, genotype/designer traits, nutrition/condition, fertility and market eligibility. Age cannot increase value without limit; desirable juveniles or viable eggs can outrank ordinary adults. Coral frags grow into colonies; tissue, polyps and living bleaching affect value. Dead organisms have zero living value; any material value is a separate physical asset, never a living sale.

One valuation service owns formulas and all tank totals. Display Base Tank Value and Current Total Tank Value = shell current value + equipment + owned rock/substrate/racks + living livestock/eligible broods + decorations. Count benthic fish once and attached corals separately from their supports. Asset totals are not spendable credits. Recompute on authoritative ticks/actions and periodic UI updates, not each visual frame. Moving livestock transfers its current value; existing acclimation stress can legitimately change that value. Keep bounded meaningful value history and correct save/reload totals.

## 16.5 Future Verified Aquarium Leaderboard — Documentation Only

The long-term end-stage goal is an online ranking by verified aquarium asset value. Preserve stable IDs and transparent formulas, but future competition requires server-authoritative ownership, transactions and valuation. Never trust browser-local save values as verified online scores. No networking, cloud account, server, online score submission or functioning leaderboard is authorized now.

''',
      '# 19. BLACK MARKET & DANGEROUS FICTIONAL CREATURES':'''## 18.5 Fixed Retail Products and Legitimate Marine Medicines

Normal livestock prices are predetermined by species/variety, offered life stage and documented grade; reopening/reloading never randomizes them. Stock may change. Current normal fish products are standard adults, existing egg products are clutches, and corals are standard unexamined frags. Medicine & Treatment is a Saltwater subcategory while all three primary tabs and permanent destination rules remain. Fixed-price products include diagnostics, appropriate quarantine parasite/ciliate/fluke care, selected antibacterial care, nutritional support, isolated coral pest care and coral environmental recovery. Each has local artwork, eligible hosts, administration, duration, stock and restrictions. Copper and other unsafe treatments must not be falsely marked reef-safe. Consumable batches occupy medical inventory, not a livestock tank. Do not expand freshwater-specific medicine/disease systems.

''',
      '# 20. QUESTS, OBJECTIVES & UNLOCKABLES':'''## 19.3 Saved Dealer Listings and Restricted Treatments

Marine dealer livestock prices may vary within bounds with rarity/scarcity, dealer behavior, condition and demand. Animals may be healthy, stressed, malnourished, infected or asymptomatic carriers; warnings communicate uncertainty without exposing exact hidden condition. Assign price/condition at listing creation, persist them, rotate only under designed inventory/dawn rules and reject stale listing submissions. Reload/open/close never rerolls a listing. Preserve limited stock, level/discovery/hours/containment and safe purchase validation. The protected pre-existing freshwater fictional specimen keeps its legacy biology and price path.

Restricted Treatments is a Black Market subcategory for fictional unregulated/experimental/counterfeit/contaminated products. Save each listing's authenticity, contamination, effectiveness, intended hidden target and host compatibility, and copy exact quality into the acquired batch and active course. Outcomes may be helpful, unresolved or harmful. Diagnosis/assay can reveal qualified findings. No real-world adulteration recipe, toxic mixture or unsafe chemical formulation is part of the game. Ownership, inventory, payment and treatment actions remain atomic/idempotent.

''',
      '## 24.1 Storage Limitations':'''### Marine Health and Market Save Extension

Preserve schema-1/schema-2 compatibility with a versioned additive marine extension: individual health/history/course state, independent medical random stream, tank exposure, legitimate stock, medicine batches, saved dealer listings/quality and value history. Migration preserves existing IDs, wallet, health, art assignments and selected aquarium. Known current extensions missing or containing invalid hidden fields are rejected and protected rather than silently regenerated. Batch/listing IDs participate in unique-identity and counter validation. Import/export/reload must not duplicate purchases, doses or hidden outcomes.

''',
      '## 26.5 Interface States':'''### Livestock and Tank Value/Medical UI

Clicking fish/coral/bottom dwellers shows species/name, age/stage, health, nutrition/stress, examined or suspected condition, relevant genes/variety, Current Value in AC and eligible dealer offer. An optional breakdown explains bounded modifiers without automatically naming an unexamined infection. Marine controls provide examination, diagnosis/treatment, appropriate quarantine transfer, medical inventory, stopping a course and restricted-batch assay. Close inspectors/resume time to advance courses. Coral Overview/Care tabs and physical placement stay functional.

Show clickable Tank Value in the main interface. Its breakdown distinguishes base shell, equipment, fish/viable broods, corals, bottom dwellers, rocks/substrate/racks and decorations, with bounded meaningful history. All stores retain the selected aquarium unless the player explicitly chooses another. Medical stock is shared inventory with declared marine eligibility, never an automatic unsafe livestock destination.

''',
      '## 27.7 UI and VIP':'''### Marine Economy/Disease Update Acceptance

Verify fixed normal retail/medicine pricing; designed dealer rotation; exact saved hidden condition/quality; individual and tank values; growth, illness, recovery and death effects; no double counting; value transfers; symptoms/progression; appropriate diagnosis and timed effective/ineffective/harmful treatment; reef contraindications; quarantine identity; stock/dose/payment idempotency and save/import protection. Repeat existing UI/art/eye/direction/coral/light/offline regressions and protected freshwater comparisons. Record measured 30/90/365-day marine scenarios without extrapolating one scenario to the entire roster.

'''
    }
    for anchor,block in inserts.items():
        assert anchor in s,anchor;s=s.replace(anchor,block+anchor,1)
    assert re.findall(r'^# (\d+)\.',s,re.M)==[str(n) for n in range(1,32)]
    mdp.write_text(s,encoding='utf8')

prefix('GAME_DESIGN.md','''The current approved milestone adds centralized marine health (`livestock-health.js`), saved dealer inventory (`livestock-market.js`), authoritative value (`valuation.js`) and strict additive persistence (`health-save.js`). It does not add livestock or online services. Normal adult/variety/egg/frag prices remain fixed by their product definitions and grade. Marine fictional dealer fish/eggs and restricted medicines get saved bounded price/condition/quality rolls at listing creation; dawn generates new listing identities. Stale submissions reject. The pre-existing freshwater fictional listing retains its legacy price/biology.

Marine fish use ich, velvet, Brooklynellosis, flukes, selected bacterial syndrome, malnutrition and environmental injury profiles. Corals have separate bleaching/tissue/pest/stress/infectious-syndrome profiles. A standard unexamined frag can acquire a saved introduction risk (5% pest roll, an additional 2% possible infectious-syndrome roll only for stony groups); these are game calibration values, not measured prevalence. Ordinary fish start healthy. Introduced contagious pressure spreads only to eligible hosts within an aquarium. Environmental/noninfectious conditions do not become contagious. Independent marine medical/dealer random streams do not advance the protected freshwater biological random stream. All 144 protected freshwater art/source files and species definitions remain byte-identical; a ten-day biological comparison matches the prior code.

Examination consumes diagnostic units. Active parasite findings use a confidence-qualified examination; carriers remain suspected. Selected bacterial diagnosis starts at 60% and requires a follow-up at least 24 game hours later to reach the 92% in-game testing confidence required for targeted antibiotics. Confidence values and times are game abstractions. Treatment is a timed individual monitored course, not real concentration dosing. Correct choice, host, confidence, severity, environment and batch quality affect recovery. Quarantine-only courses cannot be moved into a reef while active. Fish-only copper/ciliate/fluke/antibacterial courses require prepared, cycled, bare adult-fish quarantine; coral dips require a separately mounted coral quarantine environment. Diagnosis does not instantly cure. Courses consume units once, may remain unresolved, and need appropriate feeding/water. Severe fish illness calls the existing mortality engine; coral HP/dead art and existing removal remain authoritative.

Normal medicines: diagnostic supplies, monitored copper quarantine, ciliate quarantine, fluke quarantine, targeted antibacterial, nutritional support, coral pest care and coral environmental recovery. Two fictional restricted products have persisted hidden target, authenticity, efficacy, contamination and compatibility. Each acquired batch copies listing quality; an active course copies it again. Assay consumes diagnostics and reveals quality without rerolling.

Asset value, retail and resale are distinct. Marine living value uses baseline × 0.85 × bounded stage/growth, HP, nutrition, disease, condition/tissue/pigment/polyps, age, traits and fertility modifiers; cap = 4× baseline. Designer baseline is its fixed variety price. Fish resale requires ≥60 HP, low disease burden and no active course; it is at most 75% of baseline and remains below retail. Fictional resale is prohibited. Dead living value is zero. Freshwater individual valuation retains the old formula. Tank totals include the reference shell (marine shell factor 1.25), capacity/condition-adjusted equipment, fish/viable broods, corals/plants, distinct benthic fish, owned rock/substrate/racks and decorations exactly once. Dead coral skeletons have no assigned material resale value in this milestone. Cache totals per authoritative state/tick, never per sprite frame; keep at most 30 meaningful marine value-history entries. Existing transfer stress can reduce value at arrival.

Save schema remains 2 with marine extension version 1. Legacy saves gain defaults/listings without changing existing wallet/IDs/health. Current invalid/missing hidden fields reject rather than reroll. New identity namespaces include listing/batch IDs. Existing readable and corrupt-save recovery behavior remains. The older phase descriptions below are historical where they conflict with this current section; the active consolidated MDP is v2.8.

Veterinary design basis: [Merck parasites](https://www.merckvetmanual.com/exotic-and-laboratory-animals/aquarium-fish/parasitic-diseases-of-fish), [UF marine ich](https://ask.ifas.ufl.edu/publication/FA164), [UF copper compatibility](https://ask.ifas.ufl.edu/publication/FA165), [UF monogeneans](https://ask.ifas.ufl.edu/publication/FA033), [Merck bacterial disease](https://www.merckvetmanual.com/exotic-and-laboratory-animals/aquarium-fish/bacterial-diseases-of-fish), [NOAA bleaching](https://oceanservice.noaa.gov/facts/coral_bleach.html), [NOAA coral syndrome uncertainty](https://floridakeys.noaa.gov/coral-disease/disease.html). Literature informs host/treatment families and contraindications; numeric game rates are not clinical recommendations. Broad coral profiles and exact isolate/rare-species responses remain provisional.

Future only: verified aquarium-value leaderboard needs server-authoritative ownership/transactions/value. Browser-local saves cannot be trusted as online scores. No accounts, networking or leaderboard was built. Invertebrate host guards are scaffolded; no shrimp/crab/snail/starfish/urchin roster or clinical profiles were added. Full corpse decomposition, complete dry setup, substrate biology, categorical morph genetics and unrelated audit gaps remain outside this approved milestone.''')
prefix('DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md','''Delivered for review: offline marine disease/diagnosis/quarantine/timed treatment, eight legitimate medicines, two fictional restricted medicines, fixed retail prices, saved marine dealer prices/conditions/quality, current livestock values, selected-tank total/base/breakdown/history and additive save compatibility. The consolidated specification is v2.8 with all 31 major sections preserved. No new livestock or online service was added. Existing approved art and freshwater definitions/art/biology are protected.

Chrome and Edge each pass 69 new acceptance checks, 68 existing system checks and 90 current store/UI checks. Clownfish art/direction/eye regression contains 7,583 passing checks and 1,792 directional cases per browser. New checks exercise actual quantity input, exam/start-course buttons, four responsive widths, legacy migration, corrupt hidden records, exact saved listing/batch quality, contraindications, recovery/failure/harm and protected freshwater biology. Evidence and remaining limits are in [ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md](ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md).

Still incomplete/deferred: species-level coral/rare-species clinical certification, more diagnoses/agents/laboratory assays, actual invertebrate livestock and host-specific treatment profiles, full decomposition/dry setup/substrate systems, online ranking, categorical designer breeding and the remaining October 12 audit work. The full game is not declared complete. Prior phase entries below describe their dates, not the current complete status.''')
prefix('CURRENT_LIVESTOCK_CATALOG.md','''Roster and art counts are unchanged: 52 fish including four benthic fish, five coral groups, 31 named clownfish records and 25 base-linked designer phenotypes; no new freshwater or invertebrate species. Marine owned individuals now have persisted nutrition/health/condition/examination/course history and centralized current asset values. Corals track living tissue, bleaching and polyp state separately from HP. Marine disease host eligibility distinguishes fish, coral/stony groups and future invertebrate guards; it is not a new roster. Freshwater individuals keep the legacy biology/disease/value model, with the shared inspector displaying Current Value.

Five specialist clownfish purchase holds and all provisional anatomy/art/scientific-name limits remain. Marine fictional dealer animals acquire a saved hidden condition at listing creation; normal coral products are fixed-price standard unexamined frags with saved introduction risk. Artwork is reused, including existing bleached and dead coral art. No new sprite or user approval was inferred. See [the update report](ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md) for verified behavior and clinical limitations.''')
prefix('UI_SPECIFICATION.md','''Main aquarium footer displays clickable Tank Value for the selected aquarium. Its modal separates Base Tank Value, Current Total Tank Value, physical shell, equipment, fish/viable broods, corals/plants, bottom dwellers, rock/substrate/racks and decorations plus bounded history. It is distinct from spending credits.

Fish/benthic and coral inspectors display Current Value and eligible dealer offer, optional valuation modifiers, nutrition/stress and confidence-qualified medical findings. Hidden conditions are not automatically named. Coral Overview/Care tabs remain; the overview adds living tissue/pigment/polyp measures, medical actions and history. Examination uses diagnostics. Diagnosis & treatment lists owned batches with host/water/quarantine restrictions and duration. Start consumes one unit, Stop refunds none. A course progresses only while simulation time runs; modal inspection pauses existing biology. Quarantine transfer filters eligible marine destinations and offers explicit valid coral mounts, preserving identity and history. Equipment offers Prepare bare quarantine habitat only for an unoccupied marine quarantine tank; normal prepare/cycle/readiness still apply.

Exactly three primary store tabs remain. Category counts are now Saltwater 8 (including Medicine & Treatment), Freshwater 7 unchanged, Black Market 7 (including Restricted Treatments). Ordinary products/medicines have fixed prices; dealer listings show persisted prices and uncertainty warnings. Medicine purchases go to shared medical inventory and preserve the selected aquarium. Medical inventory shows units/batches; restricted quality stays undisclosed until an assay. Freshwater-specific medicine/disease controls were not added. Existing X/Escape/focus/scroll/backdrop/responsive behavior remains.

The obsolete bubbled quantity handler is now limited to its original buyFish form, avoiding the modal conflict. Quarantine/treatment transfer checks reject unsafe water and active-course reef bypasses. New medicine previews use locally drawn bottles/diagnostic kit forms in the existing store illustration system; no animal art was replaced. The older UI phase descriptions below are historical; complete dry construction, substrate biology, comprehensive inventory and illustrated VIP tiers remain unfinished.''')
prefix('BALANCE_REPORT.md','''Retail is deterministic per normal product/variety/grade. Marine black-market rolls use bounded dealer/scarcity/demand/condition multipliers, persist on listing creation and refresh at dawn; old listings reject after rotation. Hidden condition and restricted medicine quality are not rerolled by viewing or reloading. Retail, owned asset value and eligible offer are distinct. Offers are capped below retail; fictional resale remains prohibited. Treatment/assay consume stock units once. No infinite purchase/resale or dose duplication was reproduced in the acceptance fixtures.

Repeated seeded marine scenario: 75 L cycled reef, one Ocellaris pair, daily pellets, weekly prepared 25% water changes, salt/food replenishment and equipment service every 60 days when needed; no quest/showcase/sale income. Starting wallet after the pair purchase: 2,640 AC.

| Simulated days | Ending wallet | Living fish | Cumulative expenses including 360 AC pair purchase | Selected tank value |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 30 | 2,535 AC | 2 | 465 AC | 1,407 AC |
| 90 | 2,214 AC | 2 | 786 AC | 1,407 AC |
| 365 | 568 AC | 2 | 2,432 AC | 1,437 AC |

Both browsers reproduce these outcomes. This is one concrete care/affordability scenario, not proof of whole-roster or every treatment strategy balance. Isolated tests additionally validate disease value reduction, diagnosis/recovery, fixed medicines, saved uncertain quality, contraindications, failed/contaminated treatment, bounded resale and exact tank-category sums. Existing acclimation stress changes an animal's arrival value and is included in transfer tests. Further rare-species/multi-tank/medicine-demand and clinical-rate tuning remain open. See [Chrome acceptance](tests/economy-evidence/chrome-results.json) and [Edge acceptance](tests/economy-evidence/edge-results.json). Older original-phase results below remain historical.''')
prefix('README.md','''The current offline build includes marine disease diagnosis and timed care, Saltwater → Medicine & Treatment, Black Market → Restricted Treatments, saved dealer risk/price rolls and separate retail/current asset/dealer values. Click a fish/coral for Current Value and health actions; click Tank Value for shell/content totals.

For fish quarantine: purchase a marine Quarantine aquarium, open its Equipment screen and choose Prepare bare quarantine habitat while it is unoccupied. Prepare and cycle its own water normally. Buy diagnostics in the Saltwater medicines tab, inspect/examine the animal, then choose Move to quarantine. Switch to that tank to start an eligible owned course. Maintain appropriate water/food and close the inspector/resume time so treatment advances. Selected antibacterial care requires a follow-up examination at least 24 game hours later. Corals need a separate cycled marine quarantine with appropriate light/flow and a permitted rock/sand/rack mounting; copper cannot treat them. No medicine is a universal cure. Prices/clinical rates are game parameters, not real dosing instructions.

Ordinary medicine purchases enter medical inventory. Restricted fictional batches can fail or harm and retain hidden quality on reload; assay consumes diagnostics. Export a JSON backup from Settings when moving folders/browsers. Existing saves migrate without erasing owned livestock, wallet or selected aquarium. No new livestock or online leaderboard was added. The future verified leaderboard is documentation only.

[Implementation, tests and limits](ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md). Current MDP: v2.8. Older phase sections below describe their historical deliveries.''')
prefix('TEST_REPORT.md','''Current marine acceptance: Chrome 69 passed / 0 failed; Edge 69 passed / 0 failed. Existing system 68/0 and current Store/UI 90/0 in each browser. Clownfish art/eye/direction 7,583/0 with 1,792 directional cases per browser. Commands: `python tests/browser_qa.py chrome --economy` (or edge), ordinary browser regression command, and `--clownfish`. [Chrome new evidence](tests/economy-evidence/chrome-results.json), [Edge](tests/economy-evidence/edge-results.json). Includes actual examination/treatment buttons and real quantity input, no runtime HTTP requests, 1440/1024/760/390px inspector checks, exact pre-update freshwater biology comparison and protected art/data hashes. More detail in the [update report](ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md).

The previous full-project audit is the dated October 12 snapshot, not a fresh audit of the new milestone. Some root result artifacts below have been rerun and superseded; new acceptance results have their own dated evidence folder. No multi-hour performance soak, Firefox, real private-save collection or clinical efficacy certification was performed.''')

p=ROOT/'FULL_PROJECT_AUDIT.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf8')
if 'Historical snapshot notice' not in s:
    title,rest=s.split('\n',1);p.write_text(title+'\n\n> Historical snapshot notice: this is the October 12 audit. The subsequently authorized [October 13 marine economy/disease/valuation update](ECONOMY_DISEASE_UPDATE_REPORT.md) changes some findings, including quantity input, transfers, living bleaching and valuation. Original checklist classifications/counts have not been re-audited. Root regression artifacts may have newer reruns; the original boundary observations remain in tests/audit-evidence.\n'+rest,encoding='utf8')

print('Integrated marine update into MDP v2.8; verified all 31 major sections; updated required project documents.')
